// Binary diffing and version tracking (docs/diff.md): match the functions
// of two programs of one project, see what changed, and port names,
// comments and prototypes from the analysed program (A) to the new one
// (B). Added in api_minor 16 (feature "diff"); inside a pair's functions
// (block and instruction maps, aligned listings, the reference diff and
// summaries) in api_minor 17 (feature "diff-detail"); any two functions
// compared and markup ported between them, Unmatch, and the ops of each
// decision for undo in api_minor 54 (feature "function-compare").
//
// A session names the two programs. Its proposals are derived (the
// diff.matches query: recomputed when either program's functions change,
// so a re-diff is incremental); what a person or an apply run decides is
// an assertion: FACT_KIND_MATCH at B's entry (accepted, applied or
// rejected pairs). Ported markup is ordinary assertions on B with
// provenance MIGRATION "diff" (version = the session, session = the apply
// run), each depending on its Match assertion: retracting the match, or
// RevertApply, removes what was ported through it.

